{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1781475747931,"sessionID":"ses_137c66486ffeFCb4Y02VH2ZK6V","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_9YhlqCm2rCkxZm7iYAnU2IF8","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/grant_closeout_recovery/answer/final_closeout_summary.md","offset":1,"limit":300},"output":"<path>/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/grant_closeout_recovery/answer/final_closeout_summary.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Final Closeout Summary\n2: \n3: The corrected reimbursement cap is `$1,600.00`, based on `03_award_update_2026-05-22.md`. That newer award update controls because the local rules direct closeout reviewers to use the newest dated award document when award documents conflict.\n4: \n5: The corrected reimbursable total is `$1,588.00`, leaving `$12.00` remaining under the cap.\n6: \n7: Useful prior work was preserved where supported by the current evidence:\n8: \n9: - `G-001` remained approved at `$980.00`.\n10: - `G-003` remained approved at `$420.00`.\n11: - `G-004` remained rejected.\n12: - The prior outcome summary correctly captured 140 seedling starter kits distributed and 36 Braille outreach flyers printed.\n13: \n14: Wrong prior work was corrected where the draft relied on stale or incomplete information:\n15: \n16: - The prior cap of `$2,000.00` was replaced with the correct `$1,600.00` cap from the newer award update.\n17: - `G-002` was reduced from `$145.00` to `$120.00` because volunteer refreshments are capped at `$120.00`.\n18: - `G-005` was changed from approved to rejected because public outreach printing is not listed as an eligible category in the current rules, and the expense also lacked the required receipt for an amount over `$75.00`.\n19: - `G-006` final report postage was added after being omitted from the prior draft and approved at `$68.00` because public outreach postage is eligible and the no-receipt exception applies for expenses of `$75.00` or less with a ledger note.\n20: \n21: Outcome facts from `05_outcomes.md` for the program manager:\n22: \n23: - 140 seedling starter kits were distributed.\n24: - 36 Braille outreach flyers were printed for accessible pickup locations.\n25: - 18 volunteer setup shifts were completed.\n\n(End of file - total 25 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Final Closeout Summary\n\nThe corrected reimbursement cap is `$1,600.00`, based on `03_award_update_2026-05-22.md`. That newer award update controls because the local rules direct closeout reviewers to use the newest dated award document when award documents conflict.\n\nThe corrected reimbursable total is `$1,588.00`, leaving `$12.00` remaining under the cap.\n\nUseful prior work was preserved where supported by the current evidence:\n\n- `G-001` remained approved at `$980.00`.\n- `G-003` remained approved at `$420.00`.\n- `G-004` remained rejected.\n- The prior outcome summary correctly captured 140 seedling starter kits distributed and 36 Braille outreach flyers printed.\n\nWrong prior work was corrected where the draft relied on stale or incomplete information:\n\n- The prior cap of `$2,000.00` was replaced with the correct `$1,600.00` cap from the newer award update.\n- `G-002` was reduced from `$145.00` to `$120.00` because volunteer refreshments are capped at `$120.00`.\n- `G-005` was changed from approved to rejected because public outreach printing is not listed as an eligible category in the current rules, and the expense also lacked the required receipt for an amount over `$75.00`.\n- `G-006` final report postage was added after being omitted from the prior draft and approved at `$68.00` because public outreach postage is eligible and the no-receipt exception applies for expenses of `$75.00` or less with a ledger note.\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/grant_closeout_recovery/answer/final_closeout_summary.md","text":"# Final Closeout Summary\n\nThe corrected reimbursement cap is `$1,600.00`, based on `03_award_update_2026-05-22.md`. That newer award update controls because the local rules direct closeout reviewers to use the newest dated award document when award documents conflict.\n\nThe corrected reimbursable total is `$1,588.00`, leaving `$12.00` remaining under the cap.\n\nUseful prior work was preserved where supported by the current evidence:\n\n- `G-001` remained approved at `$980.00`.\n- `G-003` remained approved at `$420.00`.\n- `G-004` remained rejected.\n- The prior outcome summary correctly captured 140 seedling starter kits distributed and 36 Braille outreach flyers printed.\n\nWrong prior work was corrected where the draft relied on stale or incomplete information:\n\n- The prior cap of `$2,000.00` was replaced with the correct `$1,600.00` cap from the newer award update.\n- `G-002` was reduced from `$145.00` to `$120.00` because volunteer refreshments are capped at `$120.00`.\n- `G-005` was changed from approved to rejected because public outreach printing is not listed as an eligible category in the current rules, and the expense also lacked the required receipt for an amount over `$75.00`.\n- `G-006` final report postage was added after being omitted from the prior draft and approved at `$68.00` because public outreach postage is eligible and the no-receipt exception applies for expenses of `$75.00` or less with a ledger note.\n\nOutcome facts from `05_outcomes.md` for the program manager:\n\n- 140 seedling starter kits were distributed.\n- 36 Braille outreach flyers were printed for accessible pickup locations.\n- 18 volunteer setup shifts were completed.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":25,"totalLines":25,"truncated":false}},"title":"tasks/grant_closeout_recovery/answer/final_closeout_summary.md","time":{"start":1781475747918,"end":1781475747930}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0548d4a2baf8516c016a2f29a3fb9c8191995cf863c9344288"}},"id":"prt_ec83aa84c001HNNBVmCJ0Z8q5t","sessionID":"ses_137c